hello I'm Tyler Lansdowne community  specialist of NetherRealm Studios and we  have some exciting news for you about  the future of mortal kombat x and  specifically online play we've listened  to you on facebook and twitter and now  it's time to announce starting on  january nineteen we will begin signups  for a close public beta for the new and  improved online play with the online  beta release of mortal kombat x we are  attempting to move away from the dynamic  input latency model towards a model that  preserves the feel of an offline game  more accurately while playing online and  maintains a consistent input response  the model we are moving towards a  similar and function to the ggpo model  and could be described as a rollback  simulate forward model this means that  our engine will no longer have to wait  for both players to agree on input  before drawing its results to the screen  this creates a smoother gameplay  experience and diminishes the feeling of  lag in online play starting Tuesday  anyone who has accrued one hour of  online play time in mortal kombat x can  sign up for the beta ad beta moral  Kombat calm now keep in mind not  everyone can be invited to participate  but as the beta moves forward we will  continue to add players to the pool only  four characters will be playable at the  beginning of the beta those characters  are scorpion sub-zero Jackie Briggs and  Johnny Cage we plan on adding more  characters throughout the beta so  hopefully you'll be able to play your  favorite combatant mortal  we are excited to bring a whole new  online experience in Mortal Kombat X and  make sure you follow at nether realm on  Twitter for more information about the  beta maintenance alerts and maybe some  beta codes we will need your feedback at  the end of each play session a short  questionnaire will pop up on the screen  simply answer the questions providing  honest and objective feedback after each  match will provide nether own studios  with very valuable information we also  encourage you to provide feedback on the  MKX forums and stream your game play  this is your opportunity to help us  collect data and continue to refine our  online experience Thanks we'll see you  online
 

